{"nodes": [{"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_lineage_warning", "label": "Vendor Lineage Warning", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L5-L17", "rationale": "aigen-pr-sourcing was supplied by an external vendor and dropped into the monorepo as a clone, not authored internally. It is a partial port of the iSourcing Laravel app rather than a clean-room rewrite, so it is unknown whether it replaced the legacy import endpoint, runs in parallel, or is scheduled in vendor production at all. Operational stance: treat upstream develop as authoritative and never assume a function is dead just because the alternative branch is enabled locally.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_pr_ingestion_pipeline", "label": "PR Ingestion Pipeline (3 Stages)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L19-L29", "rationale": "Documented explicitly because stage 2 (this worker) is routinely confused with stage 1 (Laravel SAP pull) and stage 3 (reminder-email cron); npm run run:cron in backend is a scheduler, not an importer.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_prpo_download_insert", "label": "prpo:download insert (Stage 1 SAP Pull)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L24-L29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_backend_cron", "label": "Backend run:cron RFQ Reminder Scheduler (Stage 3)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L26-L29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_kafka_consumer_entrypoint", "label": "Kafka Consumer Entry Point (worker.js)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L35", "rationale": "Subscribes to KAFKA_TOPIC_IMPORT_PR (default aigen-import-pr-events) and shuts down gracefully on SIGINT/SIGTERM so in-flight DB transactions are not orphaned.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_cli_entrypoint", "label": "CLI One-Shot Entry Point (app.js)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L36", "rationale": "Runs the same two-step flow as the Kafka handler without needing Kafka; the npm alias aigen:import-pr does NOT forward --last-period-days, so lastPeriodDays silently falls back to LAST_PERIOD_SYNC.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_handler", "label": "AIGEN_IMPORT_PR_REQUEST Event Handler", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L38-L46", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_aigen_sourcing_service", "label": "AigenSourcingService", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L50", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_data", "label": "importPRData (Step 1)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L52-L53", "rationale": "Skips PRs already present in rfq_library so existing PRs never re-enter the pipeline. This creates the 'lines that had a PO at import time never get an rfq_library row' gap, which was deliberately addressed at the iSearch read layer via the matrix_cs_aigen fallback rather than by changing the skip.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_sync_rfq_data", "label": "syncRFQData (Step 2)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L54-L58", "rationale": "Wrapped in a single DB transaction and ends with TRUNCATE TABLE pr_library, so re-running while a previous run is in progress is unsafe. Only groups whose summed value falls BELOW the config_auto_po threshold get an RFQ; above-threshold groups go the auto-PO route.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_submit_rfq", "label": "_submitRFQ", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L58", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_send_email_rfq", "label": "_sendEmailRFQ", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L58", "rationale": "Error handling was rewritten to error.response?.data ?? error.message (2026-06-15) because a network-level failure returns no HTTP response, so reading error.response.data threw a TypeError that escaped syncRFQData before its TRUNCATE.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_send_email_received", "label": "_sendEmailReceived", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L58", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_get_material_assignment", "label": "_getMaterialAssignment Cascade Resolver", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L53", "rationale": "Resolves to the most-specific level whose ROW EXISTS (material_number to extended_material_group to material_group), falling back to a parent only when the child row is absent. Existence, not vendor presence, drives the cascade so an intentionally vendor-less row can express 'manual sourcing' without being overridden by a parent.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_get_pr_vendor_and_cs_by_vendor_matrix_assign", "label": "_getPrVendorAndCSByVendorMatrixAssign", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L14", "rationale": "Annotated in source as '// old method, same on isourcing laravel app' \u2014 direct evidence that the legacy CS/CL resolution was copied across from the iSourcing Laravel app rather than rewritten.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_get_matrix_category_by_sub_category_id", "label": "_getMatrixCategoryBySubCategoryId", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L100", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_select_cl_user_by_cs_id", "label": "selectCLUserByCSIdWithMaterialGroup", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_assign_cs_cl_method", "label": "ASSIGN_CS_CL_METHOD Runtime Switch", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L15-L17", "rationale": "Both CS/CL resolution paths are kept alive behind an env flag (default material_assignment) so the vendor port retains parity with the iSourcing Laravel app during migration. Consequence: a bug fix to one branch must be evaluated against the other before it is deemed safe to skip.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_vendor_matriks_assign", "label": "vendor_matriks_assign Resolution Path (Legacy)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L86", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_material_assignment", "label": "material_assignment Resolution Path (Default)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L53", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_manual_sourcing_optout", "label": "Manual Sourcing Opt-Out (null vendor)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L53", "rationale": "A material_assignment row that exists but carries no vendor_direct and no aggregator returns null, meaning 'manual sourcing, do NOT import' \u2014 the PR deliberately stays in iSourcing. It must NOT fall back to the parent level, otherwise an explicit manual-sourcing decision would be silently overridden by a broader default.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_pr_library_staging", "label": "aigen.pr_library Staging Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L57", "rationale": "Intentionally ephemeral: TRUNCATEd at the end of every successful syncRFQData cycle. Nothing that must be retained may live here; historical queries belong against rfq_library.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_rfq_library", "label": "aigen.rfq_library Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_rfq_counters", "label": "aigen.rfq_counters RFQ Number Allocation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L56", "rationale": "Single-row counter (id 1) producing RFQ + 7-digit zero-padded numbers; centralising allocation in one row is what makes the duplicate-RFQ staging leak visible as a numbering anomaly.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_config_auto_po", "label": "config_auto_po Value Threshold", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L55-L56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_server_group_value_column", "label": "Server-Group Value Column (BCG convert_value / GEMS value_idr)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L55", "rationale": "Each server group compares a different monetary column against the same threshold, so currency/normalisation differences between BCG and GEMS are handled by config rather than by branching code.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_duplicate_rfq_leak", "label": "Duplicate RFQ Staging Leak", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L58", "rationale": "A throw inside _submitRFQ escaped before the TRUNCATE, stranding staging rows that merged into the NEXT run's new RFQ number. Symptom: the 2nd RFQ holds the prior run's items plus the new ones while the 1st RFQ is left with status_vendor NULL. Root cause was reading error.response.data on an undefined response during a network-level email failure; fixed 2026-06-15 by optional-chaining guards.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_abandoned_prpo_writeback", "label": "Abandoned prpo Write-Back Approach", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L60", "rationale": "The fix/aigen-pr-pic branch (2026-05-07 to 2026-05-11) added _writeAigenCsToSearchLibrary, _writeSourcingStatusHeader and _computeSourcingState to push PIC and state into prpo.search_library.aigen_cs_pic and prpo.sourcing_status. Abandoned because (a) the vendor EasyMorph ETL truncate-inserts prpo.search_library, putting any new column at risk, and (b) the legacy iSourcing writer prpo:isearch TRUNCATEs sourcing_status \u2014 fundamentally incompatible with a second writer. Replaced by a read-side JOIN.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_isourcing_source_data_view", "label": "aigen.aigen_isourcing_source_data Live View", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L60, L98", "rationale": "Chosen over a write path so there is no AiGen-to-prpo write coupling: prpoapi/SearchController JOINs the live view at query time, and because the view reads rfq_library directly it sees PRs immediately after RFQ generation with no further worker action.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_isearch_pic_feature", "label": "iSearch Missing PIC (Issue 2)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L98", "rationale": "Resolved 2026-05-11 purely as a read-side change in prpoapi surfacing per-line PIC and a 2-state header (Completed / On Progress); no write-side code lives in this worker.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_multi_role_migration", "label": "Multi-Role Identity Migration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L99", "rationale": "Moves user identity to aigen.users plus user_matrices. Once it is the source of truth the legacy CS-to-CL lookup must switch its connection from isourcing to aigen and join user_matrices \u2014 or the legacy branch can be deleted outright if material_assignment becomes the only supported path post-rollout.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_main_sub_pic", "label": "Main/Sub PIC N-Cardinality", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L100", "rationale": "If sub-CS becomes N-cardinality, categories_matrix and material_assignment resolution return multiple sub-CS users; today the code arbitrarily picks one (materialAssignment.sub_category), so the resolvers would need to return an array and persist all of them.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_log_sla_gaps", "label": "Log & SLA Gaps (Issue 1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L101", "rationale": "PR import, RFQ-number generation and CS/CL assignment are state changes that may belong in aigen.log_activity, but the worker writes nothing there today. Instrumentation should only be added where the user's own event mapping lists these transitions.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_database_fanout", "label": "Three-Connection Database Fan-Out", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L62-L78", "rationale": "Three logical MySQL connections against a single server: aigen (read + write), isearch (read-only), isourcing (read-only). The worker writes ONLY to the aigen schema; prpo and task_board are strictly read-only from here, which is what makes the read-side iSearch integration safe.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_connection_label_mismatch", "label": "Connection Labels vs Real DB Names", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L70, L141", "rationale": "connection('isearch') actually targets prpo and connection('isourcing') targets task_board_27 (dev) / task_board (prod). Sequelize reads the real name from .env at runtime, so code need not encode the dev/prod split \u2014 only inline cross-DB SQL elsewhere in the repo does.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_search_library", "label": "prpo.search_library (SAP PR Snapshot)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L69, L75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_sentry_init_order", "label": "Sentry Init-Order Requirement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L90, L143", "rationale": "lib/sentry.js must be required before any other app module in every entry point so instrumentation hooks are installed before the modules they patch are loaded; any new entry point must preserve that ordering.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_configuration", "label": "Worker Environment Configuration (dotenv)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L80-L90", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_import_pr_claude_internal_branch_policy", "label": "internal/<feature> Branch Policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L105", "rationale": "Internal features are built on private internal/<feature> branches off the vendor's develop and are never pushed upstream, keeping the vendor-authored baseline cleanly separable from internal work.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "aigen_import_pr_claude_kafka_consumer_entrypoint", "target": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_handler", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L35-L38", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_handler", "target": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_data", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L35", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_handler", "target": "aigen_import_pr_claude_sync_rfq_data", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L35", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_import_pr_claude_cli_entrypoint", "target": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_data", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L36", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_import_pr_claude_cli_entrypoint", "target": "aigen_import_pr_claude_sync_rfq_data", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L36", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_import_pr_claude_aigen_sourcing_service", "target": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_data", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L50-L52", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_import_pr_claude_aigen_sourcing_service", "target": "aigen_import_pr_claude_sync_rfq_data", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L50-L54", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_data", "target": "aigen_import_pr_claude_search_library", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-import-pr/CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "L52", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_import_pr_claude_import_pr_data", "target": "aigen_import_pr_claude_pr_library_staging", "relation": "shares_data_w